      "label": "(i)",
      "marks": 6,
      "answer": "$AB^2=BC^2=85$ (so the triangle is isosceles) and the exact area is $34$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "1. $AB^2=6^2+7^2=85$, $BC^2=2^2+9^2=85$ ($\\to$ isosceles) — B1B1 — or $AB=BC=\\sqrt{85}$.\n2. $AC^2=8^2+2^2=68$ — B1.\n3. $M=(2,-2)$, or $BM^2=(\\sqrt{85})^2-(\\tfrac12\\sqrt{68})^2$ — B1 — $M$ is midpoint of $AC$.\n4. $BM=\\sqrt{2^2+8^2}=\\sqrt{68}$, or $\\sqrt{85-17}=\\sqrt{68}$ — B1.\n5. Area $\\triangle ABC=\\frac12\\sqrt{68}\\sqrt{68}=34$ — B1.",
